            r2_title: `Round 2 — Monday 5 April 2027: the company's order and the first employee`,
            r3_brief: `The crests and logos are now half the work and the embroiderer is late. A computerised embroidery machine costs Q36,000 at Máquinas Quetzal. Banco Pinabete lends it at 1.5% a month over 24 months to a registered business with six months of books and declarations; Don Chepe lends it tomorrow at 10% a month with no papers; Máquinas Quetzal sells it on credit at Q44,000 in twelve instalments. At this pace the workshop's sales for 2027 will pass Q150,000 in September.`,
            r3_note: `Deliverable: the machine and your answer to the ceiling. This round is scored on July–September; the ceiling bites in October–December.`,
            r3_title: `Round 3 — Monday 5 July 2027: the machine and the ceiling`,
            r4_brief: `The school-uniform season and the snow-pea season arrive together: orders for October–December are about twice the workshop's capacity. In December the law requires the aguinaldo for every worker, registered or not.`,
